What do folks think of the alchemy they added to nethack in 3.1.0?

You dip one potion in another.  The one you're dipping into is used
up, the one you're dipping does the following:

   1/8 times turns into water
   2/8 times turns into sickness
   1/8 times turns into a random potion
   4/8 times evaporates

(unless the one your dipping into is healing/extra healing, and you
 dip a nasty potion in.  In that case the nasty potion turns to water. 
 Also, don't try this if the potion is cursed)

Seems to me that it's too costly (uses too many potions -- even if they're
useless, they could have been turned into holy water), unlikely to produce
a good result, and totatly unpredictable. The best result you could possibly
achieve is basically polymorphing one of the two potions (much easier to do 
with a wand of polymorph).

I think this should be changed to be more useful.  Perhaps when you mix two
potions, if your luck is greater than 0, the resulting potion should be 
one which is more expensive than either of the two you started with (but
less expensive than their total value).  Perhaps add a slight chance of
them evaporating, but basically give you something useful to do with a 
potion of speed (if you're already fast) and a potion of levitation (if
you already have a ring): turn them into a potion of gain ability.

